# Every route in the app is prerendered to a real file (see
# scripts/prerenderRoutes.mjs), so the SPA catch-all this file used to hold
# is no longer needed:
#
#     /*    /index.html   200
#
# That rule made EVERY unmatched URL return the homepage with HTTP 200, so
# /any-typo-at-all looked like a real page to Google. Search engines call
# that a soft 404 and treat it as a quality problem.
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves /404.html with a real 404 status for unmatched
# paths automatically, so no rule is needed here at all. If a new route is
# ever added to App.jsx, add it to scripts/prerenderRoutes.mjs too or it
# will 404 on direct navigation.
